When you call a function by value :
A copy of the arguments is made and stored in the functions stack frame.
So, the function works on the copy not the original.

if you call :
x = 10
f(x)

Inside thhe function :
It receives a copy of 10.
Changing the copy does not change x in main.

How it works in memory ?
Pass by value creates :
A new memoy location in functions stack frame.
The original variable stays in the callers stack frame.
Modifying the parameters only changes the copy.

